      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Climate and Weather: Utah roofs face heavy mountain snow, ice dams, high winds, and intense UV exposure. Metal sheds snow efficiently and resists fire, while architectural asphalt shingles offer solid wind and impact performance at a lower entry price.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              4,
              5
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Long-Term Value: While asphalt requires replacement every two decades or so, a quality metal roof can often outlast two generations of asphalt shingles, evening out the lifecycle cost if you stay in your home long-term.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              0,
              3
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Installation and Contractors: Asphalt replacement is common and handled by almost any local roofer (such as ReRoofIt). Metal roofs require specialized sheet-metal installers or exterior contractors (such as B&D Architectural Metals or C Buxton Exteriors).",
